    "result_text": "All tests pass. The project's only test class (`AcceptanceTest`, 3 tests) is green, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional, validated-when-present `postcode` support for owners:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (`type: string`, `pattern: \"^[0-9]{4}$\"`, not in `required`). The pattern makes Bean Validation reject a malformed postcode (e.g. `\"12\"`) with **400** before the controller runs, and the field flows into both `OwnerFieldsDto` and `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `postcode` column with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it automatically on input and output (so it's stored and returned).\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `postcode` column. `hsqldb` (the test profile) uses `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be added explicitly.\n\n4. **`InvalidPostcodeException` + handler** in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` \u2014 returns **400** with `errors: [\"postcode\"]`, matching the existing exception-handling style.\n\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added `validatePostcode(...)`, which:\n   - skips validation when postcode is absent/blank (backward-compatible),\n   - looks up the region range via the owner's derived locality (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20112099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20113099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20114099),\n   - accepts any 4-digit postcode when the city has no known region (`UNKNOWN`),\n   - rejects out-of-range postcodes with 400.\n\nThe three acceptance tests \u2014 stores a valid postcode, accepts an owner without a postcode, and rejects a malformed postcode \u2014 all pass, and every earlier requirement's minimal (postcode-less) owner remains valid.",
